{"person_id":"fe-011-03-harj-taggar","name":"Harj Taggar","cohort_group":"Founders / operators","category":"Startup founder / investor","birth_year":1985,"age_at_milestone":23,"milestone_by_age_26":"Co-founded Auctomatic (YC W07) and sold it to Live Current Media in 2008 for approximately £2.5m at age 22-23, making him one of the youngest YC founders to achieve an exit.","early_history_summary":"Taggar attended the University of Oxford to study jurisprudence but left in 2006 to move to Silicon Valley and pursue entrepreneurship. He co-founded Auctomatic in 2007 with his brother Kulveer and Patrick and John Collison, was accepted into Y Combinator's Winter 2007 batch, and sold the company one year later. Despite being non-technical, Taggar learned to code during the YC program.","primary_leverage_engine":"Network / capital","normalized_primary_engine":"Network / capital","secondary_engine":"Complementary team","started_serious_reps_before_20_score":0,"prior_reps_score":0,"scarce_skill_depth_score":0,"native_distribution_score":0,"elite_ecosystem_network_score":2,"complementary_team_score":2,"structural_wave_score":2,"concentration_intensity_score":1,"capital_safety_score":0,"domain_proximity_score":1,"total_leverage_score":8,"success_tier":3,"leverage_evidence_confidence":"Medium","family_context_summary":"Not documented in reviewed sources. Taggar attended Oxford University, suggesting a strong educational background, but family financial or domain details are not available.","parent_family_domain_summary":"Not documented in reviewed sources.","early_family_financial_platform_support_score":0,"parent_family_domain_advantage_score":0,"inherited_audience_business_network_score":0,"elite_institution_performance_pipeline_score":1,"frontier_geography_ecosystem_score":2,"rare_early_tools_facilities_score":0,"dedicated_mentor_coach_tutor_score":1,"exceptional_peer_cofounder_sibling_score":2,"early_online_platform_community_score":0,"direct_customer_domain_exposure_score":1,"prodigy_physical_edge_score":0,"adversity_constraint_catalyst_score":0,"inherited_access_stack_count":5,"exceptional_inherited_access_count":2,"all_documented_early_condition_count":5,"primary_early_advantage_archetype":"High-trust peer team","primary_early_advantage_tags":"Y Combinator, Silicon Valley, Collison brothers, online marketplaces, startup accelerator","evidence_summary":"Taggar's key advantage was entering the Y Combinator ecosystem at its early stage (Winter 2007 batch) and co-founding Auctomatic with Patrick and John Collison (who later founded Stripe) and his brother Kulveer. The team was accepted into YC despite being non-technical, with Taggar learning to code during the program. Auctomatic was acquired by Live Current Media for approximately £2.5m in 2008, when Taggar was 22. His Oxford background provided educational credibility, but his primary leverage came from the YC network and high-quality co-founders.","early_advantage_evidence_confidence":"Medium","source_count":4,"primary_source_url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harj_Taggar","source_urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harj_Taggar","https://www.ycombinator.com/people/harj-taggar","https://www.oxfordmail.co.uk/news/2175113.graduates-sell-business-millions/","https://techcrunch.com/2012/05/30/y-combinator-harj-taggar-interview-video-tctv/"],"annotation_status":"subagent_researched_beta","source_audit_status":"not_independently_audited","data_version":"0.3.0-trajectory-beta","eligibility_status":"age_26_eligible","starting_point":"Born in 1984 or 1985; attended University of Oxford to study jurisprudence before leaving to pursue entrepreneurship. Family background not documented in reviewed sources.","current_position":"Managing Partner at Y Combinator; previously co-founded Triplebyte (YC S15) and Auctomatic (YC W07); co-founded Initialized Capital with Garry Tan and Alexis Ohanian.","current_position_year":2025,"is_living":true,"trajectory":[{"year":2006,"age":21,"event":"Left Oxford law school to move to Silicon Valley and pursue a startup idea that became Auctomatic."},{"year":2007,"age":22,"event":"Co-founded Auctomatic with brother Kulveer and Patrick and John Collison; accepted into Y Combinator's Winter 2007 batch."},{"year":2008,"age":23,"event":"Auctomatic acquired by Live Current Media for approximately £2.5m, making him one of the youngest YC founders to exit."},{"year":2010,"age":25,"event":"Joined Y Combinator as its first non-founder Partner, advising and selecting startups."},{"year":2011,"age":26,"event":"Co-founded Initialized Capital, an angel investment fund, with Garry Tan and Alexis Ohanian."},{"year":2015,"age":30,"event":"Co-founded Triplebyte, a technical hiring platform, funded by Y Combinator's Summer 2015 batch."},{"year":2020,"age":35,"event":"Returned to Y Combinator as a Group Partner after running Triplebyte for several years."}]}
